From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:26:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: desktop start-up, no exec or shell, single texture

riscosplatform.cpp: stdout and stderr to the file named by TORCS$Log
(else /dev/null; printing from a Wimp task opens a command window),
opened once and shared with dup2; a crash report (RISC OS error and
UnixLib's backtrace). The directories the Linux launcher passes default
to <Choices$Write>/TORCS and <TORCS$Dir>; the settings files are copied
on the first run (as setup_linux.sh does) and the game runs in its data
directory.
main.cpp: multitexturing off unless -M (one texture unit keeps Mesa's
software renderer on its fast textured-triangle path).
fg_gm.cpp: no X11 game mode. screen.cpp: changing the screen settings
saves them and quits with a message (no execlp), and the Display menu
offers window sizes from 320x240. telemetry: no sh.
TORCS_STATIC_MODULES builds the same start-up on Linux, to test the
static modules on a host.
---
 src/libs/tgfclient/fg_gm.cpp        |   8 +-
 src/libs/tgfclient/screen.cpp       |  24 +++
 src/linux/main.cpp                  |  25 ++++
 src/linux/riscosplatform.cpp        | 222 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/modules/telemetry/telemetry.cpp |   4 +
 5 files changed, 279 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/linux/riscosplatform.cpp

